Arithmetic requirements

Do not use ordinary floating point as your proof backend.

Use one of:

exact rationals throughout, when feasible;

interval arithmetic with outward rounding, then export rational upper bounds;

Arb/ball arithmetic is ideal.

A good design is:

core evaluation in Python calling mpmath or Arb-backed wrappers for exploration;

final certification done with exact rationals or rigorous interval bounds;

export a .lean or .json artifact with rational numerators/denominators.

The final object Lean checks should contain only rational inequalities.

